 "answer_raw": "It takes roughly **5 years** for the hybrid to break even on fuel alone.  \n\nDriving 14,000 mi/yr, Car A (24 mpg) uses about **583 gal** a year, while the hybrid (48 mpg) uses **292 gal**.  \n\nAt $3.40 per gallon, that’s about **$1,983** per year for Car A versus **$992** for the hybrid—an annual fuel saving of **$991**.  \n\nThe price gap is **$5,000** ($27,000 – $22,000). Dividing the gap by the yearly savings gives **5.0 years** of pay‑back on fuel.",
